    {
        "content": "<p>xia-chao <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14988#issuecomment-6438182926\">commented</a> on <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14988\">PR #14988</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>one helper is fine. but p2 still looks up authority in p2/types.rs, and that's the 500 on a non-ASCII Host -- <code>let _ = authority</code> isn't dedup. also the serve tests send no Host, and rfc 9112 3.2 makes that a client must, so i fixed the client, not the server.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 635328668,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793093011
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"memo\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4dd\" role=\"img\" title=\"memo\">:memo:</span> xia-chao submitted <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14988#pullrequestreview-5665599440\">PR review</a>.</p>",
        "id": 635344907,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793096956
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> xia-chao created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14988#discussion_r4387577457\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>can't be just <code>let _ = authority;</code> -- for the 400s the helper returns <code>Err</code> and it has to go through <code>tx</code> or serve sends 500.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 635344908,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793096956
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>xia-chao deleted a <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14988#issuecomment-6438182926\">comment</a> on <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14988\">PR #14988</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>one helper is fine. but p2 still looks up authority in p2/types.rs, and that's the 500 on a non-ASCII Host -- <code>let _ = authority</code> isn't dedup. also the serve tests send no Host, and rfc 9112 3.2 makes that a client must, so i fixed the client, not the server.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 635345579,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793097101
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"memo\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4dd\" role=\"img\" title=\"memo\">:memo:</span> pchickey submitted <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14988#pullrequestreview-5672433043\">PR review</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Thanks, this restructure helps a lot, I have just a couple more notes for how we should test this to make it super clear we covered all the bases</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 635483570,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793126852
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> pchickey created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14988#discussion_r4392719587\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Feels off to require a byte slice argument but return a String, it could return a Vec&lt;u8&gt; and the comparisons can still be <code>.starts_with(b\"HTTP ...\")</code>.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 635483571,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793126852
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> pchickey created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14988#discussion_r4392694273\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I don't see any reason to check for the HTML contents in these these tests, the starts with status line is sufficient</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 635483572,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793126852
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> pchickey created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14988#discussion_r4392681538\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>This could be folded down to <code>if let Err(e) = get_request_target(...) { let _ = tx.send(Err(e));  wasmtime::bail!(...) }</code></p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 635483573,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793126852
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> pchickey created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14988#discussion_r4392756753\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Lets restructure these tests: we want to test that, for a given set of requests that check one positive case and various negative cases for the the host headers, both the p2 and p3 implementations of wasmtime-wasi-http handle it properly. So, lets make a single function <code>async fn test_rfc_9112_sec_3_2(&amp;WasmtimeServe) -&gt; Result&lt;()&gt;</code> that sends all the requests and asserts the responses are what we want, and then invoke it in just two <code>#[tokio::test] async fn pN_cli_serve_rfc_9112_sec_3_2() -&gt; Result&lt;()&gt; { ... }</code> , one of which uses P2_CLI_SERVE_HELLO_WORLD_COMPONENT and the other uses the P3_ one. </p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 635483574,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793126853
    },
